# Hutchinson / Wright delayed logistic equation   x'(t) = r x(t) (1 - x(t-1))
# Equilibria x=0 and x=1.  Linearization at x=1:  u' = -r u(t-1)
#   Hopf at r = pi/2 = 1.570796 with omega = pi/2 (period 4).
#   Characteristic roots at r=1.7:  0.0563472328 +- 1.605870228 i
#                                  -1.524487644 +- 7.657465906 i ...
# AUTO needs x(0) exactly on the equilibrium (x(0)=1).  For a simulation
# change x(0) to e.g. 0.5 (it is also the constant history for t<0):
# decaying oscillations for r<pi/2, growing -> periodic orbit for r>pi/2.
par r=1.0
x'=r*x*(1-delay(x,1))
x(0)=1.0
@ total=60,dt=0.01,delay=1,meth=rungekutta,xlo=0,xhi=60,ylo=0,yhi=3,bounds=1000
@ parmin=0.5,parmax=3,autoxmin=0.5,autoxmax=3,autoymin=0,autoymax=3
done
